# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# INTENTIONAL MANUAL EXCLUSION (no ignore patterns — do not auto-gitignore):
#   src/screens/auth/
#   src/services/supabase.ts
# Deferred-scope scaffolding (Supabase / LOCK-016 / LOCK-018). Kept untracked
# on purpose until an explicit Project Owner decision to commit them when the
# Supabase phase opens. Absence of ignore rules here is deliberate, not an
# oversight — agents must not add patterns for these paths without Owner OK.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# A P2 ladder report from a DIRTY worktree records a state no sha names, so it cannot be
# reproduced and is not evidence. The clean run at the committed sha is the record.
reports/p2/*-dirty.json

# The same rule for the P4 ladder, for the same reason and on the same authority. P4's runner
# writes reports/p4/<sha>-dirty.json when the worktree is not clean, and a report that names a
# tree state no commit holds cannot be reproduced by anybody, including the session that wrote it.
reports/p4/*-dirty.json

# The render harness writes this on every gate run and the gate consumes it in the SAME run —
# it is an intermediate, not a record, and committing it would leave the tree permanently dirty.
# The durable record is the sha-named ladder report beside it, which E5 requires to be committed.
reports/p2/render-harness.json
